# Line endings: repository and working tree are LF-only.
# CRLF in the tree was an artefact of editing on a Windows host. text=auto keeps binaries
# binary, and eol=lf makes checkouts LF too, so pull/push is LF whatever a contributor's
# own git config says about line endings.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Files that are part of the repository but are NOT part of a distributed package.
#
# Consumers install destrofer/helper-library as a GitHub zipball, and git archives - what GitHub
# and Packagist serve - honour export-ignore. (Verified against symfony/console's published zipball:
# no Tests directory, although the repository has one.) `composer archive` additionally honours the
# archive.exclude list in composer.json.
#
# Note: unlike .gitignore, an attribute pattern does not recurse into a directory, and a recursive
# pattern does not match the directory entry itself - hence both lines.
tests export-ignore
tests/** export-ignore
